sec("oop", "OOP and design", "oop", [
 ("Abstraction means:", "Showing what an object does while hiding how", "Bundling data with methods", "Deriving one class from another", "Having many forms", "Encapsulation bundles and protects; abstraction hides complexity behind an interface."),
 ("A class with two direct base classes uses:", "Multiple inheritance", "Multilevel inheritance", "Hierarchical inheritance", "Hybrid composition", "Multilevel is a chain A → B → C."),
 ("In C → B → A (C derives from B, B from A), constructors run in the order:", "A, B, C", "C, B, A", "B, A, C", "Only C", "Bases are built first; destructors run in reverse."),
 ("Two overloaded functions cannot differ only in:", "Return type", "Number of parameters", "Parameter types", "const-ness of a reference parameter", "The call site gives no way to choose by return type."),
 ("A pure virtual destructor:", "Must still have a definition", "Cannot exist", "Makes the class final", "Is called only for the base", "Derived destructors call it, so it needs a body."),
 ("Protected members are accessible:", "In the class and its derived classes", "Everywhere", "Only in the class itself", "Only in friend classes", "Private is the class only; public is everywhere."),
 ("Composition differs from aggregation in that with composition:", "The whole owns the part's lifetime", "The part can belong to many wholes", "There is no relationship", "Inheritance is used", "A house and its rooms (composition) vs a team and its players (aggregation)."),
 ("Square inheriting from Rectangle with independent setWidth/setHeight is the classic violation of:", "Liskov substitution", "Single responsibility", "Open/closed", "Interface segregation", "Code expecting a Rectangle breaks when width and height are forced equal."),
 ("Single responsibility principle:", "A class should have one reason to change", "A class should have one method", "A program should have one class", "Each method takes one parameter", "Split classes that change for different reasons."),
 ("Which pattern lets you swap an algorithm at run time?", "Strategy", "Singleton", "Facade", "Prototype", "For example different payment or sorting strategies behind one interface."),
 ("Which pattern adds behaviour by wrapping an object in another of the same interface?", "Decorator", "Adapter", "Proxy", "Builder", "Stackable wrappers; Java I/O streams are the classic example."),
 ("Which pattern converts one interface into another that clients expect?", "Adapter", "Decorator", "Facade", "Command", "A plug adapter: same job, different shape."),
 ("Which pattern builds a complex object step by step?", "Builder", "Factory method", "Prototype", "Observer", "Useful with many optional parameters."),
 ("Which pattern creates objects by cloning an existing one?", "Prototype", "Builder", "Singleton", "Flyweight", "Avoids costly construction or subclassing creators."),
 ("Which pattern gives one simple interface to a complex subsystem?", "Facade", "Proxy", "Composite", "Mediator", "For example one 'placeOrder' call hiding inventory, payment and shipping."),
 ("Which pattern controls access to an object through a stand-in?", "Proxy", "Adapter", "Decorator", "Bridge", "Lazy loading, access checks, remote objects."),
 ("Which pattern turns a request into an object, enabling undo and queues?", "Command", "Strategy", "Iterator", "State", "Each command has execute() and can store what undo needs."),
 ("std::unique_ptr:", "Has sole ownership and can be moved but not copied", "Can be copied freely", "Counts references", "Never frees memory", "shared_ptr counts references; weak_ptr observes without owning."),
 ("Two objects holding shared_ptrs to each other leak because of:", "A reference cycle; fix one side with weak_ptr", "Double deletion", "Slicing", "A missing virtual destructor", "Neither count reaches zero."),
 ("RAII means:", "A resource is acquired in a constructor and released in the destructor", "Resources are freed by a garbage collector", "Every class needs an init() method", "Exceptions are disabled", "Locks (lock_guard), files and memory are released automatically, even on exceptions."),
 ("The rule of five adds which two to the rule of three?", "Move constructor and move assignment", "Default constructor and destructor", "Two comparison operators", "swap and clone", "Copy constructor, copy assignment and destructor were the original three."),
 ("A const member function:", "Cannot modify non-mutable data members", "Cannot be called on non-const objects", "Is always inline", "Must be static", "Mark mutable for caches or mutexes."),
 ("Calling a virtual function inside a base-class constructor calls:", "The base-class version", "The most-derived version", "Nothing (it is ignored)", "A pure virtual stub always", "The derived part does not exist yet during the base constructor."),
 ("operator<< for printing a class is usually a non-member (often friend) because:", "The left operand is the ostream, not your class", "Members cannot return references", "Friends are faster", "It must be virtual", "A member would need obj << cout."),
 ("Good design aims for:", "Low coupling and high cohesion", "High coupling and low cohesion", "High coupling and high cohesion", "No classes at all", "Classes focus on one job and depend little on each other."),
 ("Dynamic binding in C++ needs:", "A virtual function called through a base pointer or reference", "A template", "An overloaded operator", "A static member", "Calling on an object by value uses its static type."),
 ("Templates provide:", "Compile-time (parametric) polymorphism", "Run-time polymorphism", "Multiple inheritance", "Garbage collection", "The compiler generates code for each type used."),
 ("A virtual function with a default argument, called through a base pointer to a derived object, uses:", "The derived body with the base's default argument", "The derived body and derived default", "The base body and base default", "Neither (compile error)", "Default arguments are bound statically, the body dynamically. Avoid defaults on virtual functions."),
 ("The Observer pattern is a good fit for:", "Notifying many subscribers when a subject changes", "Creating a single global instance", "Adapting old interfaces", "Building objects in steps", "Event listeners and pub/sub are observers."),
 ("In Java a class can:", "Extend one class and implement many interfaces", "Extend many classes", "Implement only one interface", "Not implement interfaces", "Java avoids the diamond problem by allowing only single class inheritance."),
])

